  "notes": [
    "Calibrator fitted on validation half B, which has a higher base rate than test (0.094 vs 0.049), so test probabilities over-predict on average. Not corrected: production has no future labels. diag_brier_prior_shift_oracle is a diagnostic that peeks at test labels.",
    "Label is a proxy (CONTEXT.md 7.3), not real PayPal disputes.",
    "SHAP values are exact TreeSHAP in raw log-odds, before calibration.",
    "Isotonic creates tied scores, so calibrated ranking metrics can differ slightly from raw ones.",
    "Use threshold_table.json by_stage for decisions: a seller scores an order at a given moment, and at checkout only the day-0 row exists. retrospective_any_time takes each order's highest-risk snapshot, which uses delivery information from after purchase and is an upper bound, not purchase-time performance.",
    "Goodwill refund (cost 10% of order value) reduces to risk > 10%, which flags most orders at low precision: a finding about the cost assumption, not a recommendation."
